1.0.0
- Initial public release of S.O.P.H.I.A. — Companion Pip-Boy Framework.
- Includes YES MAN, FISTO, KL-E-O, MK II Stealth Suit, and Andy / Mister Handy.
- Adds modular custom installation: each large companion voice bank is optional through storageOptional.
- Companion menu dynamically shows only voice banks actually installed on the device.
- Keeps the small 51-entry IDX files in the core so each optional website selection is one complete voice-bank choice.
- Adds contextual companion voice responses across supported STATS, ITEMS, DATA, and mode-switch menus.
- Uses one active companion at a time with same-visit no-repeat protection.
- Preserves silence for MAP, STATUS RAD, RADIO/FM, and protected audio/video playback.
- Includes the hardware-tested memory-safe launcher/service baseline and UI-responsive chunked voice extraction.
- Keeps readable APP.JS source and a separate compact APP.MIN.JS runtime entry.
- Removes the legacy UI-global knob callback and legacy Yes Man service alias while preserving the required resident S.O.P.H.I.A. service lifecycle.
